-----Original Message-----
From: Baltic Shipping Claims <balticship@balticship.example>
Sent: Friday, 02 October 2026 10:30
To: Katarzyna Zielinska
Subject: Re: Damage claim CLM-2026-0912 - 14 pallets electronics Gdynia-Rotte=
rdam

We have reviewed claim CLM-2026-0912 and regret that we must reject it. Accor=
ding to the loading record, the pallets were only stretch-wrapped, with no to=
p cover or moisture barrier. Under our terms of carriage, sensitive electroni=
cs must be packed to withstand normal humidity during sea transport. We there=
fore consider insufficient packaging to be the cause of the damage, and the c=
arrier is not liable.

If you disagree, please send additional evidence within 14 days, in particula=
r photos of the packaging before loading and any independent inspection repor=
t.

Best regards,
Baltic Shipping Claims
Short-sea carrier Gdansk

-----Original Message-----
From: Katarzyna Zielinska <k.zielinska@corp-europe.example>
Sent: Tuesday, 29 September 2026 15:05
To: Baltic Shipping Claims
Subject: Damage claim CLM-2026-0912 - 14 pallets electronics Gdynia-Rotterdam

We are filing a cargo damage claim for the shipment that left Gdynia on 25 Se=
p and was discharged in Rotterdam on 28 Sep (container MSKU4471826, delivery =
80412257, PO 4500318842). On opening the container this morning, the receivin=
g team found 14 of 22 pallets of electronics wet. Cartons are soaked at the b=
ottom and sides, and several have mould spots already. Water marks on the con=
tainer wall suggest ingress from above, not from our loading.

Invoice value of the 14 damaged pallets is EUR 8,200. Please register the cla=
im under CLM-2026-0912 and confirm the surveyor appointment. The goods are qu=
arantined in Rotterdam and we will not scrap anything before the survey. Phot=
os are shown below.

Best regards,
Katarzyna Zielinska
Site coordinator Gdansk
Corp Europe B.V. | Rotterdam
T +31 10 802 4608

